#. engine/messages/register_check.py (ticket 19b): with no drawing list, a gap in a Discipline's numbering (m0-screens 6.3's "no drawing list; numbering runs 01–57; 14 and 31 missing").
msgid "engine.register_check.gap"
msgstr "No drawing list, and the numbering skips from {after} to {before}: {missing, plural, one {# number is} other {# numbers are}} missing. Until the drawing list is pasted or the consultant confirms {missing, plural, one {that sheet was} other {those sheets were}} sent, this Discipline's sheets have one source."

#. The drawing list against the sheets, both ways: m0-screens §5's Question title, verbatim.
msgid "engine.register_check.not_found"
msgstr "{number} is on the drawing list but in no file"

msgid "engine.register_check.not_listed"
msgstr "{number} is in a file but not on the drawing list"

#. The drawing-list dialog's refusals (m0-screens 6.10), for the QS who pasted or typed the list. "to" and the examples are what the QS types: the dialog reads only the English "to", so keep them as they are in every language.
msgid "engine.register_check.nothing_found"
msgstr "No line starts with a sheet number, so there is no list to use. Start each line with its number, as in S-01 General notes, or type a range, as in 01 to 57."

#. "to" is what the QS types: keep it as it is in every language.
msgid "engine.register_check.range_backwards"
msgstr "Line {line}, {first} to {last}, runs backwards. Type the lower number first: {last} to {first}."

#. "to" is what the QS types: keep it as it is in every language.
msgid "engine.register_check.range_hyphen"
msgstr "Line {line}, {first}-{last}, could be one sheet's number or a range. For a range, type {first} to {last}; for one sheet, add its title after the number."

#. "to" and the example are what the QS types: keep them as they are in every language.
msgid "engine.register_check.range_mixed"
msgstr "Line {line}, {first} to {last}, is not one range: its two numbers are written differently. Give each run of numbers its own line, both ends written alike, as in A-01 to A-29."

msgid "engine.register_check.range_too_long"
msgstr "Line {line}, {first} to {last}, holds more than {limit, number} sheet numbers, more than any drawing list. Check its first and last numbers."

msgid "engine.register_check.text_too_long"
msgstr "This is longer than a drawing list: Vextrus reads up to {limit, number} characters. Paste the list on its own, without the rest of the email."

msgid "engine.register_check.too_many"
msgstr "This names more than {limit, number} sheets, more than any drawing list. Paste only this Discipline's list."
